        "description": {
            "value": "<p><strong>Cost</strong> nothing · <strong>Requirements</strong> You are in <strong>Severance</strong></p><hr /><p><em>Frozen Heavens Hundred Flower Funeral.</em> Snow falls and ice flowers bloom on everything it touches.</p><p><strong>30-foot emanation</strong>, basic Fortitude, <strong>cold</strong> damage.</p><p>Creatures that fail are <strong>restrained</strong> in a pillar of ice (Escape against your Reiatsu DC) and take <strong>4d6 persistent cold</strong> that allows <strong>no flat check</strong> to end while restrained.</p><hr /><p><em>Canon: the target's life ends when the hundredth petal falls.</em></p><hr /><p><strong>Waning.</strong> The damage is <strong>20d6</strong> if used in the first round of Severance, and two dice fewer each round after &mdash; 18d6, 16d6, 14d6, 12d6, 10d6, and <strong>8d6</strong> in the seventh. After the seventh round this cannot be used at all.</p><p><strong>Using this ends Severance</strong>, whether you want it to or not.</p>"
